# FLOQR production cutover requirements

Resume: `@cutover$` / `$floqr-app$` (old tag `$floqr-com$` still resumes this file).

**Chosen FUTURE canonical production origin (owner decision Oct 29 2026, whole product):** `https://www.floqr.app`  
**Not switched yet — PLANNING ONLY.** Owner, Oct 29 2026: "I am not ready to switch to the floqr.app domain." GitHub Pages (`https://jadzadco.github.io/shoutout-demo`) stays the live origin until the owner says go. Until then do **not** change served code, Functions, link builders, `FLOQRCanonical` constants, preview-email bases, or OAuth / App Check config toward floqr.app.  
**Apex redirect (required at cutover):** `https://floqr.app` → `https://www.floqr.app` (301).  
**Not canonical:** `www.floqr.com` / `floqr.com` (previous choice, superseded Oct 29 2026 — may 301 to `www.floqr.app` if the owner keeps the domain), `floq.ai`, `floqr.ai`, GitHub Pages `https://jadzadco.github.io/shoutout-demo` (staging / demo only until cutover).

This file is persistent agent memory for any work that hardcodes origins, OAuth redirects, privacy links, preview emails, App Check, or hybrid deep links. VIP booking / embed / API links (VIP-P-13) use the same host — there is no separate VIP origin.

Accounts, keys, and DNS records for this host are configured through the accounts management profile (`config/accounts-profile.local.json` → `scripts/seed-accounts-profile.js`). See `design-notes-accounts-profile.mdc`.

## Can the domain be prepared before cutoff?

**Yes — and it should be.** Preparing `www.floqr.app` before cutover does **not** flip live traffic.

| Before cutoff (safe) | At cutoff (traffic flip) |
|---|---|
| Register / renew `floqr.app` (`.app` is HSTS-preloaded — HTTPS only, certificate required from day one) | Point DNS (Azure DNS or registrar) at the production host |
| Add `www.floqr.app` (+ apex) to Firebase **Authorized domains** | Make www the live hosting target (Azure Static Web Apps or Firebase Hosting) |
| Register OAuth redirect URIs for Google / Microsoft / Facebook on the new host | Leave Pages as staging / backup only |
| Create reCAPTCHA / App Check keys for `www.floqr.app` | Swap client config / secrets to prod keys if separate |
| Code: single `FLOQRCanonical` helper (no hardcoded github.io in new work) | Update SendGrid / Stripe / Twilio callback + link bases |
| Draft Privacy Policy / DNS URLs as `https://www.floqr.app/privacy.html` | Publish policy live on that host |
| Hybrid: Associated Domains / App Links for `www.floqr.app` | Ship store builds pointing at prod |

Until the DNS / hosting flip, patrons keep using GitHub Pages; account-level prefs in Firestore travel with the user. Browser CMP cookies will **not** — plan a one-time privacy re-ack or rely on `privacyPolicyVersionAccepted` on `users`.

## Agent rules (every change)

1. **Do not** invent a second production brand origin. New links, emails, VIP booking/embed/API links, and privacy copy use relative paths or `FLOQRCanonical` / `FLOQRNav` (which keep resolving to the live Pages origin until go). Write `https://www.floqr.app` only in planning docs, cutover checklists, and the accounts profile until the owner says go.
2. **Do not** hardcode `jadzadco.github.io/shoutout-demo` in new features. Use `FLOQRNav` / `FLOQRCanonical` with the staging override for Pages. Pages stays staging until cutover — do not change github.io behavior early.
3. **Display / Xibo URLs** stay `display.html?location=` / `display2.html?location=` with **no** `?v=` — only the **host** changes at cutover (`https://www.floqr.app/display.html?location=…`).
4. Page links never carry `?v=` (owner decision Oct 10 2026) — on Pages or on the new host. Only asset tags (`<script src>` / `<link href>`) are cache-busted, by the bump script. Old `?v=` URLs keep working (ignored).
5. Privacy / CCPA / Consent Mode work assumes the final policy URL `https://www.floqr.app/privacy.html` (path may adjust; **host must be www.floqr.app**).
6. Preview-email / diagnostics defaults that still point at github.io are **staging**; at cutover they switch to `www.floqr.app`.
7. Hybrid native: deep links and universal links target `www.floqr.app`, not Pages.
8. Admin / Master / staging subdomains (if the admin fork ships): `admin.floqr.app`, `master.floqr.app`, `staging.floqr.app` — same registrable domain, listed in the accounts profile DNS section.
9. Mail sender addresses (`login@floqr.com` in Functions) are a **SendGrid sender-domain** decision, not the web origin. Move them to `floqr.app` only after that domain is authenticated in SendGrid (accounts profile `sendgrid.senderDomain`).

## Code still on www.floqr.com (switch only when the owner says go — not before)

Leave these untouched while planning. On go, change them together on `main` + workspace in one change: `floqr-canonical.js` (`PRODUCTION_ORIGIN`; `isProductionHost` should accept `.app` and legacy `.com` during transition), `privacy.html` (3 strings), `ai-diagnostics-service.js` (privacy check `includes` + release note), `functions/privacy-compliance.test.js` (asserts the constant), `functions/ad-functions.js` `RETURN_ORIGINS` (add `https://www.floqr.app`). The `functions/` files must land on `origin/main` together with the workspace copy (`check-functions-sync.js`), then a Pages publish.

## Pre-cutoff checklist (do early)

- [ ] Domain registrar: `floqr.app` owned; www + apex plan documented (Azure DNS zone or registrar DNS)
- [ ] TLS certificate ready for www and apex (`.app` requires HTTPS)
- [ ] Firebase Auth → Authorized domains: `www.floqr.app`, `floqr.app`
- [ ] Google Cloud OAuth client: JS origins + redirect URIs for `https://www.floqr.app`
- [ ] Microsoft / Facebook (and any other) IdP redirect URIs updated
- [ ] reCAPTCHA Enterprise / App Check site allowlist includes `www.floqr.app`
- [ ] Stripe Customer Portal / Checkout return URLs allow `www.floqr.app`; Connect redirect URIs registered
- [ ] SendGrid link branding / sender domain decided (`floqr.app`, or keep `floqr.com` for mail only)
- [ ] Twilio status callbacks / messaging links use the new host where applicable
- [ ] POS partner OAuth redirect URIs (Square / Toast / SpotOn / Clover) registered on `https://www.floqr.app/…`
- [ ] Codebase: `FLOQRCanonical.PRODUCTION_ORIGIN` = `https://www.floqr.app`; grep clean of new github.io hardcodes
- [ ] Privacy Policy + Do Not Sell URLs written for `www.floqr.app`
- [ ] iOS Associated Domains + Android App Links files planned for `www.floqr.app`
- [ ] Accounts profile seeded (`node scripts/seed-accounts-profile.js --apply`) and its manual checklist ticked

## Cutover day checklist

- [ ] DNS live; `https://www.floqr.app` serves the app
- [ ] Apex `floqr.app` → www 301 (and `floqr.com` / `www.floqr.com` → `www.floqr.app` 301 if kept)
- [ ] Smoke: email / phone / WhatsApp / Google / Microsoft sign-in on www
- [ ] Smoke: SOS2FA, Stripe return, VIP booking link, preview links, Club Admin, Display boards (host only)
- [ ] Update Functions defaults: preview email base, any absolute URL builders
- [ ] Master Admin / diagnostics "live test URL" lines → www.floqr.app
- [ ] Club website iframes: tell clubs to re-copy the embed (host changed)
- [ ] Optional: privacy policy version bump → force re-ack once
- [ ] Monitor Auth unauthorized-domain errors for 24–48h

## Post-cutoff

- [ ] README / STANDARD-AFTER-DEPLOYMENT live URLs → `https://www.floqr.app`
- [ ] Deprecate GitHub Pages as production (keep as emergency staging only if desired)
- [ ] App Store / Play listings + privacy nutrition labels use `https://www.floqr.app`
- [ ] Counsel: Privacy Policy controller contact matches the floqr.app brand entity

